Wrote the first automated tests with node:test.

⚠️ Error / Problem Faced

Some bill totals were off by one paisa, and the total changed depending on when we rounded.

In JavaScript, 0.1 + 0.2 gives 0.30000000000000004, so calculating with decimal rupees added tiny errors.

When the GST came to an odd number of paise (for example 45,747 paise), it could not be split equally into CGST and SGST.

The command node --test test/ also did not find our test files.

✅ Resolution
Changed every money calculation to whole paise (integers).
Converted paise to rupees only when displaying amounts.
Calculated CGST = tax ÷ 2 (rounded) and SGST = tax − CGST, so the two always add up exactly.
Changed the test command to use a pattern: node --test "test/**/*.test.js".
Verified with tests that every bill adds up exactly.

